460171

1. Description
Enhance the Outage Verification process by introducing a new tigoStatus attribute at the main Outage Verification record level.
The tigoStatus attribute will represent the composite outcome of all individual generator verification results.
The composite status will be calculated based on the following priority order:
INVALID: If at least one generator has an INVALID outcome.
FAILED: If at least one generator has a FAILED outcome and none are INVALID.
QUESTIONABLE: If at least one generator has a QUESTIONABLE outcome and none are INVALID or FAILED.
SUCCESS: If all generators have a SUCCESS outcome.
INVALID: Default status if none of the above conditions are satisfied.
2. Change Description
Added a new tigoStatus attribute to the Outage Verification record to represent the composite outcome of individual generator verification results.
3. Change Details
Implemented composite status calculation logic to evaluate all generator-level OUTCOME values and determine the overall tigoStatus based on the defined priority order: INVALID, FAILED, QUESTIONABLE, and SUCCESS.
The calculated tigoStatus is populated at the main Outage Verification record level, providing a consolidated representation of the generator verification results.

